Package: remoteflow
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/michaelou/RemoteFlow
Depends: libc6, libgcc-s1, libstdc++6, libfontconfig1, libx11-6, libice6, libsm6, libsecret-1-0, fonts-dejavu-core, libicu78 | libicu76 | libicu74 | libicu72 | libicu70, libssl3t64 | libssl3
Recommends: gnome-keyring, xdg-utils
Description: Desktop workspace for the machines you administer
 RemoteFlow keeps SSH sessions, SFTP browsing and transfers, and remote file
 editing in one place. Connections live in folders with tags and favourites,
 and terminals open as tabs beside them.
 .
 Everything stays on your own computer: there is no account to create and no
 server behind it. The only request RemoteFlow makes that you did not
 configure is an optional update check.
 .
 Remote Desktop is Windows-only and is not available in this package; an RDP
 connection points you at FreeRDP or Remmina instead.
